The phrase **“standard detector cooling”** most likely includes the routine pre-run cooldown sequence if that sequence is part of the instrument’s normal operating procedure. It would generally cover:

- initial cooldown before a scheduled run;
- maintaining detector temperature during operation;
- routine automated purge/cooling cycles.

It would not necessarily cover:

- emergency or recovery cooling after a fault;
- extended cooldown caused by user error;
- nonstandard maintenance or commissioning;
- unusually high cryogen consumption outside normal operating parameters.

The agreement’s definitions, instrument SOP, or fee schedule control. If none specifies the distinction, record the pre-run cooldown as **standard detector cooling—included under base fee; no separate charge**, and do not classify it as a tank swap or specialty-cylinder use.

