If you want to avoid escalating the message, omit “APS” and simply say “the appropriate protective and legal resources.” But **do not say you caused a seizure, admit wrongdoing, threaten Colin, or accuse him of theft as an established fact.**

Filing an APS report now is reasonable based on the unexplained payments and pressure surrounding them. It does not require you to decide that Colin committed a crime. The urgent parallel task is verifying and securing your father’s medication.

